m getting  infected or getting symptoms from the  south african variant  but they're very effective at preventing  you from dying from the south african  or needing hospitalization and again  that's the key thing  so we may have to update our vaccines to  get higher levels of efficacy  but the fact is they do protect you  against what's important severe disease  you mentioned novavax and johnson  johnson we've been talking about  astrazeneca is out there potentially  we once we expand to having more  vaccines available how does that change  the strategy of vaccinations  the strategy will change in that we'll  have a bigger menu we'll have much more  capacity so hopefully  you'll see vaccination clinics be able  to schedule much more farther into the  future  have not as many concerns about supply  and when you're talking about vaccines  like the astrazeneca vaccine the johnson  johnson vaccine that don't require that  same kind of storage requirement  you can get this vaccine closer to  people you can vaccinate for example in  doctors offices or in drug stores where  they don't have access to  a cold chain so it will really make a  major difference in how quickly we can  get vaccine into the arms of americans  and also the world because the johnson  and johnson and astrazeneca vaccines are  important vaccines for the world because  think about how hard it is to maintain a  cold chain  in parts of the developing world where  there isn't access to electricity  until we can get everybody or that  majority vaccinated  we need to worry about masks still and  the cdc has obviously said on mass  transit now they want to see those masks  worn it will be mandatory  what should we know about mass going  forward we've talked a lot in the last  week week and a half about the idea of  wearing two masks also right now  well mass are the simplest way to  prevent spread of this infection and  it's something we should have been doing  better from  from the very beginning there was a lot  of data that we didn't have at the  beginning of the pandemic about the  effectiveness of mass but now it's very  clear  that masking does decrease transmission  but the thing is not every mask is  created equal some people wear flimsy  masks basically trying to check a box to  get into a store they're wearing a  bandana for example  and in that situation it does make sense  to have a multi-layered mask which might  be  achievable if you double up but if  you've got an adequate mask one that's  multi-layered that's kind of  comports with what the cdc has on their  website i don't necessarily think you  have to wear a double mask but  this all really underscores the need to  have standards for the general public  to understand which mass are adequate  which ones are inadequate and i do think  those standards are coming so we will  get better  mass for the general public and it will  be critical because this is the easiest  way  to stop this virus including its  variants from transmitting  dr amish adalga thank you
 

